From: surface-kit
Subject: backends/sprite: Show a dot for the pen instead of the arrow

Like on Windows, the pen (and the eraser) shows a small dot where it
points instead of the standard cursor shapes (arrow, text cursor,
hand...), whether an app or the shell (top bar, dock, desktop) asks for
them. Done where a tablet sprite's cursor reaches the renderer, so it also
covers the moment before an app has set a cursor. A hidden cursor stays
hidden and an app's own cursor image, such as a brush outline, is kept;
the mouse is unchanged. The dot is drawn here at the output scale.
MUTTER_PEN_DOT=0 in the environment turns it off.
---
--- a/src/backends/meta-sprite.c
+++ b/src/backends/meta-sprite.c
@@ -23,7 +23,14 @@
 #include "backends/meta-backend-private.h"
 #include "backends/meta-cursor-tracker-private.h"
 
+#include <math.h>
+
+#include "backends/meta-cursor-xcursor.h"
+#include "backends/meta-logical-monitor-private.h"
+#include "backends/meta-monitor-manager-private.h"
+#include "clutter/clutter-mutter.h"
 #include "clutter/clutter-sprite-private.h"
+#include "cogl/cogl.h"
 
